<title>CANADA: Canada's Chretien says Zaire mission still on.</title>
<headline>Canada's Chretien says Zaire mission still on.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada is determined to press ahead with the international rescue mission for Central Africa despite the mass return of refugees to Rwanda, Prime Minister Jean Chretien said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The mandate is still the same. We have to go there and we have to go for humanitarian purposes,&quot; he told reporters. The U.N. Security Council on Friday authorized an international force to help refugees return and facilitate aid deliveries.</p>
</text>
